flags={n:{'explanation':f'Restore ordinary word/quantity and punctuation spacing across this item, including repeated explanation/misconception fields and any local qualification. Concrete examples: {examples}. Preserve actual Python identifiers, string literals and valid mathematical subscripts; this is prose proofreading, not blind text replacement.'} for n,examples in spacing.items()}
def add(n,k,text):flags.setdefault(n,{})[k]=flags.get(n,{}).get(k,'')+(' ' if k in flags.get(n,{}) else '')+text
add(1,'distractors','All three distractors are sweeping guarantees or wholesale removal of task/data/models/safety needs, making the correct bounded statement trivial. Replace at least two with credible representative-data, rule-maintenance, model-capacity or distribution-coverage misconceptions.')
add(3,'distractors','The alternatives assert no numeric image representation, universal speed dominance, or every rule becoming false on each new input. Use realistic competing reasons for difficulty, such as unavailable expertise, inadequate coverage or an incorrect feature representation, while keeping knowledge-to-rule translation uniquely best.')
add(4,'distractors','The two alternatives requiring every rule to be deleted or forbidding any reuse are effectively overlapping absolute versions of the same mistake. Use distinct credible maintenance choices, such as adding an overbroad keyword rule versus preserving the unchanged list; keep the source-overstatement qualification.')
add(7,'distractors','The win-prize trigger is absent and a no-spaces error is not a credible Python string-membership outcome. Replace these with realistic substring/tokenization/return-value confusions rather than unrelated trigger or input-validity claims.')
add(8,'distractors','All wrong options rely on an invented product whitelist, impossible lowercasing or skipping the whole loop. Use plausible exact-phrase-versus-token or semantic-matching misconceptions; the current key and missed-spam interpretation are sound.')
add(9,'distractors','The nearest-neighbor/threshold alternative is unrelated to the printed formatting expression. Replace it with a credible width, alignment or slice-endpoint interpretation.')
add(22,'distractors','Two incorrect choices repeat unsupported network-transfer claims (cloud upload and sending labels to every robot). Retain one source-wording trap and use a distinct fit-versus-predict or features-versus-targets misconception for the other.')
add(25,'distractors','Programming language, numeric storage type and wheels-versus-arms are all unrelated to the learning-feedback taxonomy. Use credible alternatives involving target labels, similarity structure, reward feedback or model family rather than three easy eliminations.')
add(32,'distractors','Discarding all labels and returning the largest feature or a random training point are weak algorithmic competitors. Use plausible nearest-neighbor step/order errors such as applying a global majority before distance selection or classifying by the nearest class centroid.')
add(48,'distractors','The incorrect import-role triplets mix obviously unrelated cloud uploading, neighbor settings, labels and plotting in several places at once. Use plausible confusion among array construction, estimator fitting, plotting and colormap selection, ideally changing one role at a time.')
add(54,'distractors','Dividing by a positive sample count changing residual signs and treating the fixed sample count as a fitted parameter are weak alternatives. Prefer realistic optimization misconceptions, such as equality of minima values, changed minimizers under positive scaling, or failing to keep n fixed.')
add(56,'distractors','Requiring a fitted line to rotate through every sample is not a credible OLS-solver interpretation. Replace it with an actual confusion about optimization objective, iterative algorithm, initialization or direct solution conditions.')
add(34,'explanation','The first step currently says “Square the coordinate differences9and16”, but the coordinate differences are 3 and 4; their squares are 9 and 16. Write that operation explicitly so the instruction does not ask the learner to square 9 and 16 again.')
add(42,'explanation','Replace “The first candidate” in justification/simpleExplanation with the actual point [0.8,60] or option ID o1. The current stored options begin with o2, and app shuffling makes ordinal option references invalid.')
add(42,'difficulty','Each option already supplies its computed distance, so finding the smallest listed value is easy. Mark easy as written, or remove the precomputed distances and require an actual multi-point calculation to retain medium.')
add(52,'sourceSupport','The explanation explicitly uses the lecture’s Ridge example to qualify the universal OLS wording, but only p794 is cited. Add inspected p787, which actually lists Ridge in the regression column, preserving the local p794 conflict qualification.')
